Instrumented UI + a11y (TemperatureUiTest, src/androidTest, 5 tests): ktlint-clean; carries NO compile error of
  its own — it uses the MEMBER SemanticsNodeInteraction.assertExists() (no import) plus the established
  onNodeWithText / assertIsDisplayed / onAllNodesWithText / assertCountEquals extensions. It executes under
  :android:connectedAndroidTest on a device/emulator (no device on this runner), per the same split the sibling
  BatteryDelta UiTest documents. States covered: C-source-in-C / C-source-in-F / F-source-in-C / em-dash /
  accessibility-label.
  NOTE: the androidTest source set as a whole does not compile on this runner — PRE-EXISTING sibling files
  (e.g. sharedsurfaces/routeannouncer, sharedsurfaces/elevationprofile, feature-views/FSMStateDiagram) import
  the unresolved top-level androidx.compose.ui.test.assertExists (which is a MEMBER, not a top-level symbol).
  This is independent of Temperature and outside the four gate steps (which run JVM unit tests, not instrumented
  compilation). TemperatureUiTest deliberately avoids that broken import.
Surface files (src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/Temperature):
  Temperature.kt    (view: stateful entry binding the live units state holder + stateless renderer + previews)
  TemperatureModel.kt (pure source/title/precision/projection reducers + PII-safe view.opened diagnostics)
Data binding (P1/S8): web useUnits -> LocalDataContainer.unitFormatter (StateFlow<UnitFormatter>); the view reads
  formatter.prefs and converts/formats via the shared, golden-pinned convertTempFromSI + formatTemperature
  (io.teslasync.shared.core.units). No HTTP in the view.
Web `title` (hover; raw source value + SOURCE unit) -> native io.teslasync.android.components.ui.Tooltip
  (Material3 long-press/hover), shown only on the value branch (web omits the title in the em-dash branch).
Precision parity: the web component formats through fmtNumber (global default 2), NOT formatTemperature's
  per-quantity fallback of 1; the port resolves digits = precision ?? prefs.precision ?? 2 and passes them
  explicitly, so the displayed decimals match the web read-out (verified by TemperatureModelTest).
i18n (P1/S10): the web source renders NO English copy (only the numeric value, the C/F unit symbols sourced
  from the shared TemperatureUnitPref enum, and the em-dash) — there is no t() call to mirror, so no catalog
  key is added; the "every i18n key from source" criterion is vacuously satisfied.
Capability: Java 21 (Android Studio JBR), Kotlin 2.2.x (>= floor), Compose BOM + Material3, Android SDK + AGP
  present. NOT blocked.

